{"_data": [{"contents": [{"type": "lesson_name", "content": ""}, {"type": "unit_name", "content": "Information Security Exposure"}, {"type": "position", "content": 9}, {"type": "origin", "content": "stub"}, {"type": "lesson", "content": 3}, {"type": "level", "content": "A2.2"}], "type": "metadata"}, {"contents": [{"type": "test", "content": "false"}], "type": "achievment_test"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "These are words you hear and use to talk about information system exposure."}], "type": "target_word_describer"}, {"contents": [{"type": "primary", "content": "Identify key information about people's jobs and places of work in spoken or written contexts.  Design the technological architecture of the IT system, through hardware and software recognition, based on available technology in the market, the analysis report and the distribution diagram."}, {"type": "secondary_1", "content": "Understands important information and aspects of attitude and intention in spoken situations in English on a range of common communicative topics related to this level."}, {"type": "secondary_2", "content": "Recognizes simple ideas on the design of an information system, computer architecture and hardware, and basic concepts on graphic design."}], "type": "objectives"}, {"type": "background_image", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob09re1img01.jpg"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<strong>First Conditional with the If Clause in Negative </strong>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "<p>There are some types of conditions in English. Some are possible, others are unlikely while others are impossible. <strong>The First Conditional</strong> is about a real condition with a possible or imagined future consequence or result.</p>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Form the <span class=\"strong\"> first conditional </span> with two clauses. One of them is the likely condition and the other clause is the imagined future consequence or result. It doesn't matter which clause you use first, but in case you begin with the conditional clause, you must place a comma at the end of the first sentence before you can begin the second sentence. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i><span class=\"strong\"> If we enforce </span> employees to follow the rules for the correct use of our information system, it <span class=\"strong\"> will </span> reduce complaints and petitions over 40% in a period of just three months.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>Enforcing employees to follow the rules <span class=\"strong\"> will </span> reduce complaints and petitions over 40% in a period of just three months <span class=\"strong\"> if </span> we <span class=\"strong\"> do </span> it for the correct use of our information system.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Conditional with If in Negative Clause</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "You use the word \u201cif\u201d to state that the condition is likely to happen in opposition to the word \u201cwhen\u201d that means the condition is more definite. In the negative form, you can express the condition with if in another way:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "If not = unless"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Examples:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i><span class=\"strong\"> If </span> we <span class=\"strong\"> don't take</span> the necessary precautions, the system might collapse for data stolen or data corruption.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i><span class=\"strong\"> Unless </span> we <span class=\"strong\"> take</span> the necessary precautions, the system might collapse for data stolen or data corruption.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i>The system <span class=\"strong\"> might </span>   collapse for data stolen or data corruption <span class=\"strong\"> if</span>   we <span class=\"strong\"> don't take</span>   the necessary precautions.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<span class=\"strong\">Grammar structure</span>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "The grammatical structure for the first conditional is pretty straightforward."}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">If/unless + subject + don't/doesn't + verb (present) + complement </div> </br><div class=\"center_text\">(Clause 1)</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<div class=\"center_text\">subject + will/may/might/can + complement</div> </br><div class=\"center_text\">(Clause 2)</div>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "Example:"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i><span class=\"strong\"> If</span> we <span class=\"strong\"> don't check</span> the security policies and guidelines, end users sooner than later <span class=\"strong\"> will complain</span> for the improper functioning of the system.</i>"}, {"type": "text", "content": "<i><span class=\"strong\"> Unless we</span> reassign authorized access to some of our employees, we <span class=\"strong\"> will keep</span> experiencing data loss and data corruption.</i>"}, {"type": "example", "content": "If the software of an information system doesn't have a defect in the programming code, hackers won't have the chance for direct access into the system to cause any harm or data loss, this is vulnerability."}, {"type": "example", "content": "For instance, unless you locate papers, a computer or any devices in the correct place, somebody will inevitably steal them and therefore the sensitive data contained there, too."}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "heading", "content": "<strong>Best Network Security Programs</strong>"}, {"type": "describer", "content": "Network security programs are tools specially designed to prevent data loss, reduce the system's vulnerability and keep the integrity, availability and confidentiality of the information.  "}, {"type": "example", "content": "One option is to promote strong password log-in into the system."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Another alternative lies on not guaranteeing access to everybody to sensitive data."}, {"type": "example", "content": "Proper data handling."}, {"type": "text", "content": "There are many network security programs available in the market used to protect an information system. Here we'll describe briefly some of the functionalities and capabilities of such programs. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "<p>Depending on the robustness and complexity of the program, they can reduce cyber-attacks when they:</p> <ul> <li>Perform log aggregation</li> <li>Perform log analysis</li> <li>Do compliance reporting</li> <li>Realize file integrity monitoring</li> <li>Monitor user activity</li> <li>Perform event correlation</li> <li>Provide real-time alerting</li> <li>Perform log forensics and log retention</li> <li>Identify root causes of security incidents and data breaches</li> <li>Also offer email encryption and email delivery proof</li> <li>Protect against third party spying</li> <li>Block access to restricted websites and isp speed throttling</li> <li>Protect users against malicious programs such as worms, trojans, viruses, hackers, spam and other ways of intrusion</li>"}, {"type": "image", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob09img01.jpg"}], "type": "learning_points"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "programming code "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "the fundamental component of a programming language that consist of written instructions used to make a machine perform a task."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: Certainly. If the software of an information system doesn't have a defect in the programming code, hackers won't have the chance for direct access into the system to cause any harm or data loss, this is vulnerability."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob09aud01"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "IT officer "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "title given to someone responsible for the company's information technology strategy and supervision of the people, technology and processes associated to it."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If the IT officer does not promote and enforce good practices, the whole system sooner or later will be into trouble. "}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob09aud03"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "password "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a personal and secret series of words and numbers used to guarantee individual access to a system, computer or program"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: One option is to promote strong password log-in into the system."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob09aud04"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "grudge "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "a feeling resentment and dislike felt for someone who has treated you badly"}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(noun)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If you guarantee former employees, who have a grudge against a company, complete access to the system without taking proper precautions, they might cause intentional harm or data loss."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob09aud05"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "name", "content": "enforce "}, {"type": "definition", "content": "to impose or make other people obey rules or policies or to be accepted."}, {"type": "part_speech", "content": "(verb)"}, {"type": "example", "content": "Example: If the IT officer does not promote and enforce good practices, the whole system sooner or later will be into trouble."}, {"type": "audio", "content": "enpe8n4le03ob09aud06"}], "type": "target_word"}, {"contents": [{"type": "text", "content": "Search for information about information security exposure. "}, {"type": "text", "content": "Identify different strategies to avoid information security exposure. "}, {"type": "text", "c